GE and set up your own 2FA before the transaction is finalized. Rushing the process increases the risk of triggering platform security alerts. A methodical, staged workflow ensures that the handover is completed without compromising the account\'s long-term integrity.</p><h3>What should I do if the seller tries to recover the account?</h3>\n<p>If you used a protected marketplace, the retained audit logs and moderated messaging history provide the evidence needed for dispute resolution. Our system tracks the credential handover and OGE transfer in real-time. If a seller attempts a recovery during the protection period, the funds remain secured until an admin review is complete. This is why you must never move the conversation to external, unmonitored apps where evidence of the agreement can be easily deleted or faked.</p><h3>Can I change the username (handle) after purchasing the account?</h3>\n<p>You can change the handle, but doing so immediately after logging in from a new IP is risky. It\'s better to wait at least 72 hours until the account recognizes your device and location as \"trusted.\" Sudden changes to the handle, email, and password in a single session are high-intent triggers for automated bans. When you buy x account with followers, patience is a security requirement. Wait until the initial handover filters have passed before rebranding the profile.</p>','A direct payment for a social media login isn\'t a business transaction; it\'s a security gamble. In 2026, the decision to buy x account with followers requires more than a handshake. Most buyers focus on vanity metrics while ignoring the underlying risks of IP flagging and \"pull-back\" scams where sellers recover accounts through support channels. You need a protocol, not just a password. This is about verified ownership, not just temporary access.\n\nWe understand the anxiety of high-stakes digital acquisitions. You want an established presence, but you can\'t afford a permanent ban or a fraudulent 