ollows a five-step progression:</p>\\n\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Move your channel to a Brand Account. This is non-negotiable for separating your personal data from the asset.</li>\\n<li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Invite the buyer as a \'Manager\'. This gives them read-only access to analytics and health metrics without any power to change settings.</li>\\n<li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Promote the buyer to \'Owner\'. This level allows them to manage content, but they cannot remove you.</li>\\n<li><strong>Step 4:</strong> The 7-day security wait. This is a mandatory cooling-off period enforced by Google\'s systems.</li>\\n<li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Final promotion to \'Primary Owner\'. Once this step is complete, you can safely remove yourself from the account.</li>\\n</ul>\\n\\n<p>Using a structured environment like the <a href=\\\"https://accsmarkets.org\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">AccsMarkets marketplace</a> ensures these steps happen in the correct order while your payment remains secured.</p>\\n\\n<h3>The 7-Day Primary Owner Rule: Your Security Buffer</h3>\\n\\n<p>Google enforces a mandatory 7-day wait before any new user can be promoted to Primary Owner. This isn\'t a hurdle; it\'s your strongest defense. This window prevents a hijacker from instantly locking you out of your own creation. You should use this time to verify that the buyer\'s payment is fully secured and that no chargeback attempts have been initiated. If you detect any suspicious activity or if the buyer pressures you to bypass this period, you still have the authority to revoke their access immediately. You are the Primary Owner until the final second of that seventh day.</p>\\n\\n<h3>Protecting Your Personal Google Data</h3>\\n\\n<p>Your personal Gmail, Google Drive, and Photos are often linked to the same identity as your YouTube channel. A Brand Account is a standalone asset that protects your personal identity. Before starting the transfer, you must 