d synergy to protect your investment. The goal when you buy telegram channel for business use is to leverage existing trust, not destroy it.\",\"question\":\"Can I change the name and niche of the channel after I buy it?\"},{\"answer\":\"Reclamation is a common risk in unmonitored P2P deals. To prevent this, ensure the transfer follows Telegram\'s official ownership migration protocol. This requires the seller to have 2FA enabled for seven days. Once the transfer is executed, the previous owner loses all rights to the asset. Using a marketplace with documented evidence trails and identity verification significantly reduces the likelihood of a seller attempting a fraudulent recovery.\",\"question\":\"What happens if the seller tries to reclaim the channel after the sale?\"},{\"answer\":\"Yes, identity verification is a mandatory part of our trust-first infrastructure. We utilize KYC and KYB integration to ensure all participants are accountable. This isn\'t about bureaucracy; it\'s about security. By verifying the identity of both buyers and sellers, we eliminate the anonymity that fraudsters rely on. This process creates a controlled environment where high-stakes digital transactions can occur with professional reliability and peace of mind.\",\"question\":\"Do I need to undergo KYC verification to buy a channel on AccsMarkets?\"},{\"answer\":\"The owner has absolute control, while an admin has delegated permissions. Only the owner can delete the channel, manage other admins, or transfer ownership to another account. When acquiring an asset, simply being added as an admin is insufficient. You must receive full ownership transfer through the app settings. This process requires a seven-day \\\"cooling off\\\" period for 2FA, ensuring the transaction is authorized and permanent.\",\"question\":\"What is the difference between an admin and a channel owner in Telegram?\"}]','<p>What if you could bypass three years of grueling content creation and start pitching to a veri