tomated lockdown is minimized. You\'re protecting the asset\'s value as much as your own payment.\\n\\n### Common Scams Targeting Sellers in 2026\\n\\nScammers have evolved. The \\\"Middleman\\\" scam is now a standard tactic. A buyer suggests using a \\\"reputable\\\" escrow agent from a specific forum who is actually an accomplice. Once you hand over the credentials, both the buyer and the agent disappear. Others use proof-of-funds fraud, providing doctored screenshots of crypto wallets or bank balances to build false confidence. Social engineering remains the biggest threat. Scammers may trick you into revealing recovery details or \\\"testing\\\" the login under the guise of verification, only to lock you out immediately. Without a moderated environment, these tactics are nearly impossible to prevent.\\n\\n### Why Traditional Payment Methods Fail Sellers\\n\\nTraditional payment systems are built for physical goods, not digital assets. PayPal and credit card providers frequently side with buyers in \\\"item not received\\\" disputes. Since you can\'t prove delivery to a physical address, you often lose the funds and the account. While crypto offers payment finality, it lacks protection for the seller during the transfer phase. You need a milestone-based protection layer to ensure the money is secured before you initiate a [secure social media account transfer](https://accsmarkets.org/blog/secure-social-media-account-transfer-5-dangerous-myths-debunked-for-2026). Relying on unverified methods is a gamble that puts your hard-earned digital equity at total risk.\\n\\n## <a name=\\\"accsmarkets-trust-infrastructure-a-professional-alternative\\\"></a>AccsMarkets\' Trust Infrastructure: A Professional Alternative\\n\\nAccsMarkets operates as a transaction-management provider, not a passive listing board. This distinction is critical for anyone looking to **sell social media accounts** without falling victim to the [prevalence of social media scams](https://www.ftc.gov