to ensure your safety. Access our verified global buyer network today. You\'ve built the value; now it\'s time to secure the profit. Treat your digital exit with the same rigor you used to build your audience. You\'re ready to transact with confidence.\\n\\n**[Start Selling Your Social Media Accounts Safely on AccsMarkets](https://accsmarkets.org)**\\n\\n## <a name=\\\"frequently-asked-questions\\\"></a>Frequently Asked Questions\\n\\n### Is it legal to sell social media accounts in 2026?\\n\\nSelling an account is not illegal under federal or international statutes in 2026. It\'s a contractual violation of most platform Terms of Service. While the platform may terminate the account if they detect the sale, financial authorities like the IRS recognize these profiles as taxable property. You\'re engaging in a private asset transfer that requires a secure environment to manage the inherent platform risks and ensure tax compliance for the sale proceeds.\\n\\n### How does AccsMarkets protect sellers from chargeback fraud?\\n\\nWe eliminate chargeback risk by using milestone-based transaction protection. When you **sell social media accounts** through our platform, the buyer\'s payment is secured by an approved provider before you ever hand over credentials. We hold these funds in a secure state until the buyer verifies the account details. This structure prevents the buyer from reversing the payment after they\'ve gained control of the asset, ensuring you receive your funds for every successful transfer.\\n\\n### What is the \\\"Original Email\\\" (OGE) and why is it required?\\n\\nThe Original Email is the specific address used to create the account. It\'s highly valued because it serves as the ultimate recovery tool. Buyers require the OGE to ensure the seller cannot \\\"pull back\\\" the account using automated recovery forms after the transaction is complete. Providing the OGE signals that you\'re a professional seller committed to a total transfer of ownership. Accounts without the OGE often face lower valuations or buyer rejection.\\n\\n### How long does the account transfer process usually take?\\n\\nTransfer timelines vary by platform and security requirements. A standard Instagram or TikTok handover can be completed within 24 to 48 hours. YouTube and Facebook transactions often take seven days due to mandatory platform cooling-off periods for changing the Primary Owner. We recommend following these native platform timelines strictly to avoid triggering automated security flags. Rushing the process often leads to account lockdowns, which can delay fund release significantly.\\n\\n### Can I sell a monetized YouTube channel if it has a strike?\\n\\nYou can sell a channel with an active strike, but you must disclose it in your listing. Strikes directly impact valuation because they increase the risk for the new owner. Professional buyers will audit your copyright status and community guideline history before making an offer. Transparent disclosure builds trust and prevents disputes during the verification phase. A channel with a clean record will always command a higher market premium than one with active violations.\\n\\n### What happens if a buyer opens a dispute after the transfer?\\n\\nIf a dispute arises, our administrators perform a manual review of the transaction audit logs. We examine the secure messaging history and the ownership evidence provided during the listing phase to determine a fair outcome. Because all communication stays on-platform, we have a factual record to resolve claims quickly. This structured oversight protects you from fraudulent \\\"item not as described\\\" complaints that are common in unmoderated peer-to-peer trading environments.\\n\\n### Do I need to undergo KYC/KYB to sell high-value accounts?\\n\\nYes, we require integrated KYC or KYB verification for all high-value transactions. This process confirms your identity or business status and helps us maintain a secure marketplace. By verifyin