ecured before you initiate this technical transfer. This structure prevents the buyer from vanishing with the account without paying.\n\n### How do I avoid scams when selling my channel?\n\nTo avoid scams, never move conversations to external messaging apps like Telegram or Discord. Scammers use these platforms to hide their tracks. Always use the **best place to sell youtube channel** inventory which provides an unalterable audit log. Avoid middleman services that lack formal KYC verification. Milestone-based workflows are essential; they ensure the buyer\'s funds are captured by an approved provider before you hand over any login credentials.\n\n### Can I sell a channel that has copyright strikes?\n\nYou can sell a channel with strikes, but it significantly reduces your valuation and buyer pool. Active strikes are liabilities that risk permanent account termination. Professional buyers will demand a steep discount or wait for the strikes to expire before closing the deal. Transparency is mandatory; failing to disclose strikes during the listing review process will lead to a failed transaction and a permanent ban from high-trust marketplaces.\n\n### How long does the channel transfer process take?\n\nThe process takes a minimum of seven days due to Google\'s technical security protocols for Primary Owner transfers. Once you add a new owner, you must wait exactly 168 hours before you can transfer full control. Total transaction time usually spans 10 to 14 days when factoring in listing verification, buyer due diligence, and fund clearance. Attempting to bypass this timeline often triggers security locks that can freeze the account.\n\n### Why should I use a marketplace instead of selling directly?\n\nMarketplaces provide the infrastructure required for high-risk digital asset transfers. Selling directly via DMs leaves you vulnerable to payment reversals and account hijacking with no recourse. A professional platform acts as a digital guardian, providing KYC verifica