What happens if the seller tries to take the account back?</h3>\n<p>Our escrow system prevents the seller from receiving payment until you have full control. If a seller attempts a recovery scam during the seven-day handover, our human moderators intervene to stop the transaction and return your capital. Once you are the Primary Owner and have updated all recovery details, the seller has no technical path to reclaim the asset.</p>\n\n<h3>Do I need a new AdSense account for the purchased channel?</h3>\n<p>You should link your own verified AdSense account to the channel once you become the Primary Owner. Relying on the seller\'s AdSense is a critical security flaw because they could redirect your earnings. Wait at least forty eight hours after the ownership transfer before you update the payment settings to avoid triggering fraud alerts.</p>\n\n<h3>Why does AccsMarkets use crypto for transactions?</h3>\n<p>Crypto settlements using USDT, BTC, or ETH offer instant verification and total privacy for Indian buyers. Traditional banking in India often involves high international fees and multi-day processing times for digital asset transfers. Crypto ensures that funds are secured in escrow the moment you decide to <strong>buy monetized youtube channel</strong> inventory.</p>\n\n<h3>How can I verify if the subscribers are real?</h3>\n<p>Check the Audience Retention and Traffic Sources reports in the channel\'s YouTube Studio. Real subscribers are driven by organic search and suggested videos. If the analytics show massive spikes in \"Direct\" or \"External\" traffic with very low watch time, the subscribers are likely botted. Genuine engagement always correlates with watch time.</p>\n\n<h3>What is the risk of the channel being demonetized after purchase?</h3>\n<p>The risk is minimal if you follow a methodical content transition plan. Demonetization usually happens when a new owner mass-deletes old videos or uploads \"Reused Content\" that violates platform policies. When you